updateDuneQuery.description:
Update an existing Dune query. Use this tool to modify a query's SQL, title, description, privacy, tags, or parameters.

When to call this tool:
- The user wants to save changes to a query they own (or have edit access to via team membership).
- Updating SQL content, renaming, changing privacy, archiving, or editing tags/parameters.

Important notes:
- queryId is required and must be the numeric ID of the query.
- Only supply the fields you want to change; unchanged fields will be preserved from the existing query.
- The tool performs an optimistic-locking update: if someone else edited the query concurrently you'll get a conflict error.
- Only change queries from private to public if the user explicitly requests it, else ask for confirmation to avoid accidental data exposure.
- Temporary status can be changed with is_temp.

Example usage patterns:
- Update SQL only:        { "queryId": 12345, "query": "SELECT * FROM ethereum.transactions LIMIT 10" }
- Rename:                 { "queryId": 12345, "name": "My Updated Query" }
- Make private:           { "queryId": 12345, "is_private": true }
- Update tags:            { "queryId": 12345, "tags": ["defi", "uniswap"] }
- Multiple changes:       { "queryId": 12345, "name": "New Name", "query": "SELECT 1", "is_private": true }
